## Hints for Future Agents
- pricing.go is the single source of truth for model rates. When a new
  Claude model drops, adding regular + :fast entries here is sufficient —
  no code changes to main.go required.
- The :fast suffix is appended in processFileForCache (main.go:551) when
  the JSONL entry's usage.speed == "fast". It's not a separate model, it's
  a pricing variant. Always add both "claude-X" and "claude-X:fast" pairs.
- calculateCostAllRegular/AllFast exist so the table can show "what would
  this have cost if everything ran regular / everything ran fast" — they
  derive from the base and :fast keys respectively. Missing either key
  silently falls back to default pricing and produces wrong numbers in
  those columns without any error.
- Ordering convention in the map: newest version first (4.7 above 4.6 above
  4.5 above 4.1), Opus > Sonnet > Haiku families, short-form aliases last.

## Codebase Discoveries
- Opus 4.6 and Opus 4.7 share both the regular and fast pricing schedules
  exactly. That's also why the short-form "opus" alias can stay version-
  agnostic — it points at the shared rate.
- Opus 4.1 (claude-opus-4-1-20250805) is on a legacy higher rate
  ($15/$75 vs $5/$25) — worth noting if ever asked to collapse Opus
  entries into a single alias; you can't without losing accuracy on 4.1.
- Model IDs for recent Opus releases dropped the date suffix
  (claude-opus-4-6, claude-opus-4-7) while earlier ones kept it
  (claude-opus-4-5-20251101, claude-opus-4-1-20250805). So the undated
  form is expected for 4.7 too.

